<article class="env-corollary" id="5C57">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5C57">Corollary <span data-tag="5C57">4.2.1.7</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category, and let $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ be any diagram. For every vertex $v$ of $\calC $, the map $\calC _{p/} \times _{\calC } \{ v\}  \rightarrow \calC ^{p/} \times _{\calC } \{ v\} $ is a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $\calC _{p/} \rightarrow \calC ^{p/}$ is a categorical equivalence of left fibrations over $\calC $; now apply Proposition <a href="/tag/81A7" data-tag="81A7">3.3.1.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>